/* book exam traps: PRF sets the unambiguous range and pulse width sets the range resolution — never the other way round. | Both formulas carry a factor 2 for the round trip, c τ ÷ 2 and c ÷ (2 × PRF). Drop it and every answer halves or doubles. | ADS-B is a broadcast, not an interrogation; nothing is sent to the aircraft to prompt it. SSR is the system that asks. | SSR asks at 1030 MHz and hears the reply at 1090 MHz. Reversing the pair is the standard one-mark trap. | More power buys detection range (radar equation), not resolution. Resolution is bought with a shorter pulse. */
