/* book exam traps: GPWS is reactive and looks down with the radio altimeter; TAWS look-ahead is predictive and needs a terrain database plus a position. Do not swap the two. | Mode 1 (sink rate) uses barometric descent rate gated by RA; Mode 5 (glideslope) needs a tuned ILS and is below-path deviation in dots. Not the same warning. | Quote radio altitude, not barometric altitude, as the gating quantity of Modes 1 to 5. A barometric height of 900 ft over high ground may be 300 ft above the hill. | FLTA is the forward-looking terrain avoidance function; the premature descent alert is a separate TAWS alert for being too low for the distance to the runway. */
